            "role": "authored-acquisition-foundation",
            "officialWholeSourceCredit": false,
            "sourceContext": "physical/printed57 module9.1 P is compulsory exclusively Leistungsfach, Lewis donor/acceptor and coordinate bonding. Page58 module9.2 W is optional; theory comparison only if optional8.7 was taught. Page36 complexometry is deepening/linkage; page29 keeps the elective pool. No individual selection is asserted.",
            "existingDependentGoalId": "e22a34d4-ac1e-5afe-8f77-0dfa4fd9f44f",
            "existingRequiresRoute": "e22a34d4-ac1e-5afe-8f77-0dfa4fd9f44f -> 363c5740-8a3c-50b8-8c3a-5548c80c36ea",
            "compilerScopeSemantics": "No applicability override or source mapping is added. The pinned actual stock compiler already includes the required jurisdiction. Compiler visibility is separate from official source coverage; these metadata fields do not enforce stage/course. Current views remain CrossStage and retain their existing GK/LK scopes.",
            "topicChoiceBoundary": "Required own foundation for an already authored target under the owner policy including authored topics before a later selector; no individual learner choice or new universal official duty is asserted.",
            "sourceLimit": "RP9.1 supports the coordinate-bonding core at LK. The whole existing Fehling/tartrate and supplied qualitative occupied-donor/unoccupied-acceptor orbital case is a declared own operational foundation, not exact official whole-profile credit. No choice of9.2/8.7 or full optional orbital/complex theory module is inferred.",
            "acquisitionScope": "Whole unchanged363c/P: ligand lone pair and supplied suitable central-ion acceptor orbital, soluble Cu(II)-tartrate purpose, coordination versus later Cu(II)/Cu(I) redox, fresh donor availability and fragment-model limits. This model explanation gives no actual Fehling experiment or EDTA titration credit.",
